WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.740
We stopped using Nano Banana
for AI Influencers,

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:05.940
because honestly,
our Krea 2 workflow looks way better.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.440
And this is the exact
master workflow we built

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.340
inside ComfyUI and every
custom node is included.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:12.860
And by the end of this video,

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.960
the whole thing is yours completely free.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.320
The workflow is simple.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.380
We don't start by comparing outputs,

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.560
we start by showing you the actual canvas,

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:24.400
because every one of these results
comes out of nodes we built ourselves,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.380
not a black box like Nano Banana.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:27.620
And here's the proof:

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:31.300
this is our raw base image straight
out of the first generation.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:32.320
And on top of that,

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.300
this workflow even pushes
Krea 2 into real 4K,

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:37.240
and Krea 2 can't do that on its own.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.420
So here's the plan.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:41.020
We'll walk the entire canvas end to end,

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:45.200
and then we'll show you exactly how to get
this complete master workflow for free,

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.340
before the free access window closes.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.100
But real quick, before we start:

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.680
you get this whole workflow
at the end of the video,

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:53.000
completely for free,

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.980
and all I ask in return is a like,

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:57.120
and a nice follow, that is the whole deal.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:59.010
Okay, so this is the whole canvas.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:01.170
About seven stages, from left to right,

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:04.110
and every single one of them
does exactly one job.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.570
And every stage has
its own switch up here,

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:07.910
so you can run the whole thing,

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:09.830
or you turn off what you don't need.

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:11.750
And here is the difference to Nano Banana.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:14.110
There, all of this
happens behind one button,

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:15.610
and you never see any of it.

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:17.470
Here, every step is on the table,

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:18.870
and every step is a node..

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:22.290
So let's start where every image
starts and that is the resolution.

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:24.350
So this is our resolution node,

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.690
and we built this one
for exactly one reason.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:28.913
You pick your aspect ratio, one to one,

00:01:28.913 --> 00:01:30.830
nine to sixteen, or three to four,

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.710
then you pick 2K or 4K,

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:34.530
and that is everything you touch here.

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:37.930
And by the way, you can use this node
with every other workflow you want.

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:40.550
And now comes the part
most people get wrong.

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:45.590
Krea 2 is trained for a maximum
of 2048 pixels per side,

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:47.110
that is the official limit.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:50.650
And if you just set 4096
in a normal workflow,

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:53.430
it still runs, but the image falls apart,

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:56.450
double faces, repeated hands and so on.

00:01:56.490 --> 00:02:00.790
Because the model sees four times more
images than it ever saw in training.

00:02:00.983 --> 00:02:02.863
And that is what this whole chain solves,

00:02:03.243 --> 00:02:05.443
not one node, but four of them together.

00:02:05.783 --> 00:02:07.483
The latent, that is the small canvas

00:02:07.483 --> 00:02:09.963
the model paints on before
it turns into pixels,

00:02:10.423 --> 00:02:12.603
gets created at full 4K right away.

00:02:12.843 --> 00:02:14.923
But the painting itself starts at 2K,

00:02:15.103 --> 00:02:16.723
the size Krea 2 was trained for,

00:02:16.843 --> 00:02:18.523
so the whole image comes out right.

00:02:18.703 --> 00:02:21.443
Then, halfway through,
our workflow doubles the canvas once.

00:02:21.743 --> 00:02:24.383
And Krea 2 finishes
the last steps at full 4K,

00:02:24.543 --> 00:02:26.323
where it only adds the fine detail.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:29.440
So it is not a 2K picture
blown up at the end,

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:34.700
Krea 2 itself finishes
the image at 3072 by 4096,

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:36.180
and you can see it right here.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:37.080
And to be fair,

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.800
Krea 2 was never made for this,

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:40.540
we just built the path around it.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:41.360
And by the way,

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:45.400
everyone inside our skool community
has instant access, to this workflow.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:46.980
And lets come to the models,

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:49.080
and this is the shortest
part of the video.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:54.120
We load Krea 2 turbo as the FP8
version then text encoder and the VAE,

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:56.500
and that is it,
everything stays on default.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:59.100
And we take FP8 for one simple reason:

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:01.300
it is the same model, just stored smaller,

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.240
so it needs about half the memory,

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:05.120
runs on a normal gaming GPU,

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:06.540
and the image looks the same.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:09.600
And if you want a version
for the INT8 Krea 2 model,

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:11.960
write it in the comments, and I build it.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.660
And now the part I really
like the most, the prompt.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:16.880
You can just write it
yourself in this field,

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.380
like in every other workflow.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.840
But we built something better,
our Auto Prompter.

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:24.300
You just drop in a few example
pictures of the look you want.

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:25.720
After that you click generate,

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:28.620
and it writes the complete
Krea 2 prompt for you.

00:03:28.817 --> 00:03:31.217
And the reason it works
this well sits right here,

00:03:31.417 --> 00:03:32.397
in the system prompt.

00:03:32.657 --> 00:03:35.257
This is everything we learned
about prompting Krea 2,

00:03:35.417 --> 00:03:37.997
how a real amateur photo
has to be described,

00:03:38.257 --> 00:03:40.317
so the result looks real and not like AI,

00:03:40.537 --> 00:03:42.117
all of our secrets are in there,

00:03:42.117 --> 00:03:44.437
and you get all of it for
free with the workflow.

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:46.107
Under it are the instructions,

00:03:46.407 --> 00:03:48.207
and that is where you
tell it what you want,

00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:50.727
like a casual selfie, or a mirror shot.

00:03:50.927 --> 00:03:52.467
And if you use a character LoRA,

00:03:52.647 --> 00:03:55.187
it puts your trigger word
in front, all by itself.

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:57.967
Then you copy the finished
prompt into the prompt field,

00:03:57.967 --> 00:03:58.707
and hit run.

00:03:58.907 --> 00:03:59.727
One thing to know:

00:03:59.867 --> 00:04:02.587
the Auto Prompter runs over the xAI API,

00:04:02.747 --> 00:04:04.627
so one prompt costs you a few cents.

00:04:04.883 --> 00:04:06.483
And this is our first image,

00:04:06.763 --> 00:04:09.683
straight out of Krea 2, already in 4K.

00:04:10.063 --> 00:04:11.983
And honestly, this is already good.

00:04:12.263 --> 00:04:14.543
The skin has texture,
the light looks real,

00:04:14.903 --> 00:04:17.443
and nothing is falling apart,
even at this size.

00:04:17.763 --> 00:04:20.123
And this is the point
where most workflows stop.

00:04:20.503 --> 00:04:22.063
But ours has two more stages,

00:04:22.263 --> 00:04:25.683
and one of them fixes the one
thing Krea 2 gets wrong most often.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.750
First, real quick,
there is a skin detailer in here too,

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:30.210
and we keep it off today.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:33.510
Because Krea 2 already gives
you good skin out of the box,

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:34.850
and if you want even more,

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:37.030
a good skin LoRA does that job as well.

00:04:37.217 --> 00:04:39.097
But the eyes, that is a different story,

00:04:39.237 --> 00:04:42.457
because eyes are the one thing
Krea 2 gets wrong most often.

00:04:42.597 --> 00:04:44.437
In a full picture the eyes are tiny,

00:04:44.657 --> 00:04:46.417
so you get a soft, blurry iris,

00:04:46.417 --> 00:04:48.137
or two eyes that don't quite match,

00:04:48.257 --> 00:04:50.497
and that is the first
thing everybody notices.

00:04:50.817 --> 00:04:51.657
So look at this.

00:04:51.837 --> 00:04:53.637
This is before, and this is after.

00:04:53.777 --> 00:04:56.077
The iris is sharp now,
the catchlight is there,

00:04:56.077 --> 00:04:58.577
and it is still exactly her eye,
just finished.

00:04:58.697 --> 00:05:00.597
And this is how our eye detailer does it:

00:05:00.677 --> 00:05:03.097
it finds the eyes on its own,
cuts them out,

00:05:03.197 --> 00:05:06.837
blows each one up to full size
so the model can finally see it,

00:05:06.937 --> 00:05:09.337
then runs three quick steps
with very little noise,

00:05:09.337 --> 00:05:11.137
so the eye stays the eye it was,

00:05:11.337 --> 00:05:12.877
and pastes it back with soft edges,

00:05:12.877 --> 00:05:14.737
so you never see where it was cut.

00:05:14.883 --> 00:05:16.163
And real talk for a second.

00:05:16.403 --> 00:05:18.063
What you see here is the free version,

00:05:18.063 --> 00:05:19.943
and it is the real thing, not a demo.

00:05:20.363 --> 00:05:24.243
But inside our skool community sits
the whole production stack around it,

00:05:24.443 --> 00:05:27.203
how we build the influencer herself,
how we train her,

00:05:27.403 --> 00:05:30.243
and how she stays the same
face in every single image.

00:05:30.503 --> 00:05:32.443
And the gap between
the people watching this,

00:05:32.443 --> 00:05:34.763
and the people inside already running it,

00:05:34.763 --> 00:05:36.563
gets bigger every single week.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.620
So, like we said at the start,

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:41.280
this whole workflow is yours,
completely free.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:45.280
Every node, the auto prompter with
our whole system prompt, all of it.

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:46.580
And here is how you get it.

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:47.760
Go to our Instagram,

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:50.960
@matrixlabai the link is
in the description for it.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:53.680
Follow us, and send us
a DM with the word Krea,

